  "question_text": "Tack-post pair, top strip: does it print braced and snap apart by hand?",
  "hypothesis": "E-014 faces were good but 1697 mm2 of fused rib/seam contact cracked the 0.65 mm backs on separation; E-011 showed zero contact lets the top wobble. 124 small tacks (4% of the contact) every 8 mm keep the bracing and break easily; 1.25 mm backs survive it.",
  "prediction": "The strip prints as cleanly as E-012's at the top, and the two halves snap apart by hand without cracking.",
  "why_this_test": "Short check of bracing and separation before committing 4 h to the deadline pair.",
